  "instructions": [
    "Heat sesame oil in a large pan over medium heat.",
    "Add Canadian turnip and cook until browned on all sides.",
    "Add soy sauce, rice vinegar, mirin, sansho pepper, salt, and black pepper to the pan.",
    "Stir to combine and bring to a simmer.",
    "Reduce heat to low and cook for 20 minutes or until the turnip is tender.",
    "Remove from heat and let cool to room temperature.",
    "Serve chilled or at room temperature.",
    "Garnish with chopped scallions or sesame seeds if desired."
